{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1477343-i-m-dense-can-someone-please-explain-the-technique-mega-edge","id":1477343,"title":"I'm dense: can someone please explain the Technique Mega-Edge?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-03-25T10:53:05-07:00","id":1477343,"title":"I'm dense: can someone please explain the Technique Mega-Edge?","content":"How does the Technique Mega-Edge work? If I buy Elemental Mastery, do I also but the Mega-Edge and apply it? I'm missing something simple, probably, and need some help.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26269-bastion-avalos","name":"Bastion Avalos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T12:29:57-07:00","id":1477352,"title":"","content":"I'm not actually sure why Elemental Mastery is a thing, since it doesn't actually seem to do anything. They spent an entire page of the book on the Elemental Mastery Power and example &quot;Elemental Themes&quot; for Elemental Mastery, but the power seems to amount to:<br /> <br /> 1). Buy a Power of your choice.<br /> 2). Cross out the name of that Power and rename it Elemental Mastery.<br /> 3). Buy some thematically appropriate Techniques.<br /> <br /> As for how Technique works, buy a Power of your choice, then buy Technique and say you're applying it to that specific Power. Total up the xp cost of the original power (ignoring any xp rebates from Transformations); this is the maximum number of points you can put into the Technique.<br /> <br /> As an example, Bakugo the Mad Bomber has Quantum Attack 3 (36 xp), which lets him fire explosive blasts from his hands. He wants to be able to fly, so he buys the Technique Mega-Edge and claims he can use his explosive blasts to propel him like a rocket. For the 12 xp it costs to buy Technique, he can get up to 36 xp to spend on the Flight power and associated Tags. Because he used Technique instead of buying Flight separately, using Flight while making a Quantum Attack is considered a mixed action, even though Flight is usually Reflexive.<br /> <br /> The rules don't specifically say it, but every time you spend xp to improve the base power, you should be allowed to improve the Technique as well. You should in fact be allowed to improve the Technique whenever you want, so long as it is within the xp budget. So if Bakugo only takes Flight 1 to start with, then boosts the Technique to Flight 2 and then Flight 3 because he's getting more proficient at flying, that is perfectly fine and good roleplaying. If he runs into trouble because he only has Flight 1, but Flight 3 would let him catch the fleeing sports car, he should probably even earn some Momentum for good roleplaying. Then he should do a training montage during his downtime, and come back the next session with a higher fight speed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","user":"Shepherdboi","date":". 03-25-2022, 03:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T16:29:50-07:00","id":1477371,"title":"","content":"Elemental Mastery is a shortcut Power, there's a few like that in the game but it's helpful to have.<br /> Basically it's like having Technique on a Power, but based on a theme. It skips the middle man. Most Elemental Masteries will start with Quantum Anima to start, representing manipulation of the theme, but really it could be anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1468-blindeye","name":"Blindeye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1468_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T18:41:21-07:00","id":1477380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blindeye</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1477343-i-m-dense-can-someone-please-explain-the-technique-mega-edge?p=1477371#post1477371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elemental Mastery is a shortcut Power, there's a few like that in the game but it's helpful to have.<br /> Basically it's like having Technique on a Power, but based on a theme. It skips the middle man. Most Elemental Masteries will start with Quantum Anima to start, representing manipulation of the theme, but really it could be anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you explain to me how it is supposed to be a shortcut, because the rules don't seem to support that. I'll give an example via Grav-Master, who has gravity powers:<br /> <br /> Version 1: Doesn't buy Elemental Mastery:<br /> <br /> Environmental Anima 2 (24 xp)<br /> Technique (Environmental Anima: Flight) (12 xp)<br /> Technique (Environmental Anima: Quantum Attack) (12 xp)<br /> total: 48 xp<br /> <br /> Version 2: Buys Elemental Mastery:<br /> <br /> Elemental Mastery 2 (Base Effect Environmental Anima) 2 (24 xp)<br /> Technique (Elemental Mastery: Flight) (12 xp)<br /> Technique (Elemental Mastery: Quantum Attack) (12 xp)<br /> total: 48 xp<br /> <br /> Where is the shortcut?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T19:21:34-07:00","id":1477383,"title":"","content":"\u201cShortcut\u201d was probably a poor choice of words. Rather, Elemental Mastery is actually an example of a Power Suite (which in turn is a fancy way of saying \u201ca Quantum Power with Techniques\u201d). It gets its own entry under Quantum Powers because Elemental themes are by far the most prominent Power Suites you're likely to encounter in the world of Aberrant (or in any superhero setting, for that matter).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-26T11:50:45-07:00","id":1477458,"title":"","content":"Basically, when you buy a power that has multiple expressions, each expression becomes a technique for purposes of point-buy. You then have a single power that can do a lot of things, but you pay for it by purchasing each thing it does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-28T03:15:09-07:00","id":1477575,"title":"","content":"As some one who has played multiple super hero games, elemental mastery is another attempt to reduce redundant power lists. Again, in other games the lists can get hilariously bloated. Every game attempts this noble feat but fails in some way or another, whether that is in lack of required specificity or too much minutia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1435-videopete","name":"videopete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-28T15:54:55-07:00","id":1477599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1477343-i-m-dense-can-someone-please-explain-the-technique-mega-edge?p=1477380#post1477380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you explain to me how it is supposed to be a shortcut, because the rules don't seem to support that. I'll give an example via Grav-Master, who has gravity powers:<br /> <br /> Version 1: Doesn't buy Elemental Mastery:<br /> <br /> Environmental Anima 2 (24 xp)<br /> Technique (Environmental Anima: Flight) (12 xp)<br /> Technique (Environmental Anima: Quantum Attack) (12 xp)<br /> total: 48 xp<br /> <br /> Version 2: Buys Elemental Mastery:<br /> <br /> Elemental Mastery 2 (Base Effect Environmental Anima) 2 (24 xp)<br /> Technique (Elemental Mastery: Flight) (12 xp)<br /> Technique (Elemental Mastery: Quantum Attack) (12 xp)<br /> total: 48 xp<br /> <br /> Where is the shortcut?</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess it's more accurate to say it's more of a thematic shorthand than a shortcut. It just helps you, as the player, get you to where you want to be faster. You're right it's indistinguishable, but it helps not to have to explain to players how to make a Fire-Bender by taking Version 1.<br /> <br /> Version 2 is easier to understand from the player-side is all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1468-blindeye","name":"Blindeye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1468_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-30T18:09:27-07:00","id":1477721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1477343-i-m-dense-can-someone-please-explain-the-technique-mega-edge?p=1477380#post1477380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you explain to me how it is supposed to be a shortcut...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a shortcut in thinking about how one puts together a character. Elemental Mastery is nothing more than <i>&quot;Pick a base Power then add Technique dots to it&quot;</i> but that doesn't spark the imagination quite so easily as <i>&quot;This power represents your control over elemental forces&quot;</i>. The power is not <i>technically</i> needed, but it is needed for <i>flavour </i>and <i>understanding the system</i>. New players especially have a much easier time envisioning Johnny Storm as having &quot;Elemental Mastery: Fire&quot; than they do &quot;Quantum Aura + Technique dots&quot;.<br /> <br /> Players also generally start flicking through the powers list when putting a character together. They get to the bit in character creation that says <i>&quot;Spend XP on these things&quot;</i> and there is no mention of Power Suites or using Technique, so they're going to forget it. My kids did and they're not super young or new to roleplaying. They simply followed (as much as possible) the process as outlined for creating their characters. Even then, because one of the characters was based on the concept of shapeshifting ala &quot;Alex Mercer / Prototype&quot;. I had to point out he could Power Suite his Morph to include Plasticity and Boost as Techniques. The telekinetic character though got it through Elemental Mastery: Kinetic Energy without any assistance needed.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-31T20:57:57-07:00","id":1477826,"title":"","content":"Another thing I forgot to mention is that &quot;Elemental Mastery: X&quot; is much easier on both the player and storyguide for purposes of <b>Power Stunts</b>.<br /> <br /> A 'Power Suite' is a mechanical-only representation of the game mechanics behind the character's construction. These powers are collected together using Technique, which means the powers cost less XP, require extra Quantum to use at the same time, and can be negated together. For inspiring power stunts though, it may as well be empty text. &quot;Elemental Mastery: Nature&quot; (as used in the power stunt example) gives the player &amp; storyguide some options &amp; boundaries on how they can use their powers' <i><b>flavour</b></i> as a jumping point for stuff they haven't explicitly bought in char-gen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T04:43:35-07:00","id":1480360,"title":"","content":"It's possible put Mega-Attributes and/or Mega-Edges in a Power Suit? In page 211, in Time Elemental Theme, say &quot;yes, its possible&quot;, but in Power Suit description and Technique Mega-Edge don't say anything.<br /> <br /> If so, multiple Mega-Edge and/or Mega-Attributes are placed together in a single Power Suite technique slot?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/437-shadowninja","name":"shadowninja","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T07:43:36-07:00","id":1480365,"title":"","content":"First, Mega Attributes are not described as possible parts of techniques, so I would say they can\u2019t be.<br /> <br /> Mega Edges are described as examples but not in the rules, so what to do with requisites? Can you accelerate a person (using the book example) to any speed? How much would it cost, as Mega Speed is a 1dot Mega Edge that is locked to Mega Dexterity, but you can\u2019t use Mega Attributes to power it? It is not so simple to make it fit the rules.<br /> <br /> I may have a house rule for that.<br /> <br /> <b>Mega-Edges Based Techniques</b><br /> Some Mega-Edges, while work perfectly as they are, could be used to represent more flexible powers, and so those Mega-Edges may be turned into techniques of other powers.<br /> It\u2019s not possible to use a Mega-Attribute that way, but as they are prerequisites of many of the Mega-Edges, the cost of the related Mega-Attribute must be considered. Each dot of Mega-Attribute required by the Mega-Edge must be bought as part of the power and will also define the Quantum Minimum of the created power, but will not grant any advantages the regular Mega-Attribute would. Mega edges that have different effects, according to the dots in the Mega-Attribute, like Mega-Speed that define scale based in the dots in Mega-Dexterity, must have the appropriate level of Mega-Attribute for the desired scale.<br /> It\u2019s possible to combine multiple Mega-Edges into a single power, if they fit the desired concept, and, if they share the same prerequisites, the dots in Mega-Attributes must be payed only once.<br /> For example it\u2019s possible to create a technique related to time manipulation to accelerate the time flow to the character and make him impossibly fast, based in the Mega-Edges Mega-Speed, Multi-Tasking and Quickness. The three Mega-Edges share the prerequisite and the progressing scale of Mega-Dexterity. To be able to act at Speed Scale 5 it requires Mega-Dexterity 4, what requires at least Quantum 4, and adding the 3 chosen 1 dot Mega-Edges, the total cost of this technique is 84 experience (equivalent to 7 dots of power), yet the Nova would not be able to use any of the advantages of Mega-Dexterity, as they are not part of the technique. As any other power, it would be possible to add tags, for example Bestow, allowing the character to accelerate others, and that cost would be added to the total cost of the technique.<br /> It\u2019s impossible to create techniques based on the Body Modification, Q-Tech and Technique Mega-Edges.<br /> Other examples of techniques would be Telepathy (based in many social Mega-Edges as a control over electromagnetic fields inside people brains), Earth Shaking (based in Shockwave as control over earth and rocks) or Cyberkinesis (based in Digital Manipulation, Digital Scan and Telecommunication as control over electromagnetic fields inside computers).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 05-07-2022, 10:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-09T05:32:42-07:00","id":1480526,"title":"","content":"The Technique Mega-Edge, RAW, only lets you buy Quantum Powers. I would assume the Mega-Edges being listed under Time Mastery are a mistake, especially because they are 1 dot M-Es. You could, for the same price, buy them outside the power suite and be able to use them with less restriction than if you bought them in the power suite.<br /> <br /> That said, not being able to apply Technique to Mega-Edges makes Mega-Edge focused characters very expensive. Your Bricks and Speedsters are going to be much more expensive to create than a Blaster. I'd be all for allowing Technique to apply to Mega-Edges on a case-by-case basis, because some builds would need it just to be viable, and some builds would be way out of control if using it. (Also, what happens if you use the Technique Mega-Edge to buy more Technique Mega-Edges?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-09T06:35:22-07:00","id":1480529,"title":"","content":"I liked much your ideas Mateus Luz, I will use this in my games.<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/437-shadowninja","name":"shadowninja","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-27T16:31:42-07:00","id":1523238,"title":"","content":"Holy undead threads, Batman! <br /> <br /> So...I backed all this *just* for aberrant and I am finally getting around to learning all this stuff and this is the same question I had. Is there any official word on why Elemental Mastery Exists? As just a way to encourage technique usage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25366-bahamut810","name":"Bahamut810","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-27T19:40:51-07:00","id":1523249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bahamut810</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1477343-i-m-dense-can-someone-please-explain-the-technique-mega-edge?p=1523238#post1523238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Holy undead threads, Batman!<br /> <br /> So...I backed all this *just* for aberrant and I am finally getting around to learning all this stuff and this is the same question I had. Is there any official word on why Elemental Mastery Exists? As just a way to encourage technique usage?</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I can guess it\u2019s only there as a placeholder to show how technique can be used.<br /> <br /> But I have a variation of Elemental Mastery that I may share:<br /> <br /> ELEMENTAL MASTERY<br /> Quantum Minimum: 2<br /> Action: Ordinary<br /> Cost: 1 Quantum point<br /> Dice Pool: Quantum + Power<br /> Range: Short<br /> Duration: Concentration<br /> Elemental Mastery, as described in the book, is not a real power, but a base to build your power suite, what can be done with any power, taking away the special meaning of Elemental Mastery. This system changes the most basic aspect of the Elemental Mastery, turning it into a very flexible power based in Power Stunts, instead of Power Suites. It\u2019s possible to add techniques to Elemental Mastery, as any other power, it just happen it\u2019s not based in it.<br /> The basic system for power stunting is, the character rolls Quantum + Power, and the successes are used to generate effects, from 1 success for a minor effect, to 4 successes for truly massive. It\u2019s possible to duplicate powers that fit the power theme, spending 1 success per power dot. The character would be able to duplicate Mega Edges, Powers and other effects.<br /> Power Stunts are very flexible, left to the\u200b Storyguide to define limits, to make this job simple, as this power will use the concept very often, some guidelines are needed. Adding tags to Elemental Mastery allow the nova to cross this limits, what is an advantage to chose Elemental Mastery instead of power stunting with other powers.<br /> The Nova must be at close range of the targeted element to be able to use it, and the effect may not last longer than the time the Nova keeps concentra- tion on it. Once concentration is broke, the element will return to its normal behavior, meaning solids may stay the way they are, fluids will flow and en- ergies will dissipate, and other elements will work as expected.<br /> The amount of targeted element is the approxi- mate size of a backpack (size 0), but energies and gases may be harder to define, it\u2019s also possible to control a small amount to affect a larger body, for example targeting a few liters of what we inside a lake may cause small waves, and stopping some air in a window may cause a flow to stop.<br /> The element must be a single body of element, controlling several drops of water is not possible, but controlling the equivalent amount as a single volume is ok. For energies it may be harder to define, but as a general rule the energies in a sin- gle object are considered a single target, so using Cold Mastery to freeze a single target is ok, but not many different targets at same time.<br /> Minor effects are effects that happen naturally to the targeted element, but would not happen in that condition, like a puddle may freeze, but not in the summer, or a wave may form, but not without cause. In the other end of the spectrum are truly massive effects, that are things that are not possible in real world, but yet the nova can do, like a plant growing many meters a matter of seconds, a rock reshaping to become a tool, water flow upstream, lava to flow out of the ground in a non volcanic area, etc. Notice that the amount of material is irrelevant, the criteria is the chances of it happening naturally.<br /> When duplicating a power, the rules work as described, each success translates into a Quantum Power rank, Power tag or Mega-Edge dot, and the use of the power stunt only gives access to the power, requiring to spend the duplicated power to use it, and it will remain available for the Elemental Mastery duration only.<br /> A Nova can\u2019t duplicate powers that are beyond their quantum capacities, let\u2019s say a Quantum 2 Nova with Rock Mastery want to change the properties of a rock, duplicating Transmutation, no matter the results in the dice, the Nova will not be able to do, because it requires Quantum 4. Also, duplicating a power may not take the effect out of the power theme, for example, using Rock Mastery to turn stone into water is impossible, because wa- ter is not in the power theme, but turning a rock into a precious stone may be possible (if the Nova\u200b has at least Quantum 4).<br /> Elemental Mastery can apply the following special power tags, but any other tag added to the power will be inherited by the duplicated power, as long as it fits:<br /> \u2022 Area (2): Allow the effect to affect a larger area.<br /> \u2022 Duration (1): The Nova don\u2019t need to concentrate to maintain the effect active, changing the duration to Maintained.<br /> \u2022 Might (1): The power\u2019s might Scale increases by 1, increasing the amount of element affect- ed by the power.<br /> \u2022 Ranged (1): Increase the possible distance between the Nova and the target of Elemental Mastery.<br /> \u2022 Multiple Effects (3): The nova can use multiple effects at same time, not requiring to dissipate the previous effect to use the power again. This tag requires at least Maintained Duration to be pick. While not affecting the rolls of other actions, each active effect reduce by 1 the number is actions possible in a mixed action, if the number of actions available is reduced to 0, the nova can\u2019t do anything but keep attention to the active effects (including not being capable of using this power again), for as long as all that effects are active.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 09-28-2023, 07:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-28T04:09:31-07:00","id":1523268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bahamut810</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1477343-i-m-dense-can-someone-please-explain-the-technique-mega-edge?p=1523238#post1523238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Holy undead threads, Batman!<br /> <br /> So...I backed all this *just* for aberrant and I am finally getting around to learning all this stuff and this is the same question I had. Is there any official word on why Elemental Mastery Exists? As just a way to encourage technique usage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Rules-wise, it's redundant. But it is in there because it is such a basic staple of the superhero genre that if it was missing, people would be wondering why.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T10:29:22-07:00","id":1523563,"title":"","content":"Elemental Mastery exists because without it there would be endless questions about how Technique works.<br /> <br /> i know this because there are endless questions about it in Mutants and Masterminds forums.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}